thank you I am here tonight as I think  all of us are first and foremost as film  fans and to publicly thank Kevin  Brownlow for a lifetime of determination  unswerving preservations  perseverance and uncompromising devotion  in order to make sure that the films  that we love we can see them forever in  the way that they were meant to be seen  so we bow down to you sir Kevin your  devotion to the audience and unshakable  belief in the silent film as an art form  is inspiring and as your fellow  archivists have recently noted your  commitment to absolute perfection in  every aspect of research writing  restoration production and exhibition  has changed film history and influenced  new generations of filmmakers every time  one of them sets out on another flea  market run or a dusty attic or garage  sale in search of that elusive missing  bit of footage the fingerprints of your  own pioneering detective work will be  casting a very long shadow you were  there first and because of that we are  all very lucky indeed the silent greats  that we saw in the previous film are  obviously no longer with us but thanks  in large part to the brilliant and  painstaking efforts of Kevin Brownlow  their immortality is assured so I'm  certain that somewhere tonight chaplain  Lloyd Keaton Chaney Garbo Gish Gant's  DeMille the door and Griffith are in  countless others are lifting a glass and  raising a toast tonight to this  remarkable man and his priceless  accomplishments on behalf of the  Academy's Board of Governors I proudly  present this Oscar with the eternal  gratitude of all those who came before  us and all those people out there in the  who will come after to Kevin Brownlow  come on and get this  you
 

